-- title:
--   Lemma 3: nonzero coefficient entries are constant within each component
-- statement:
--   Fix positive integers $n,m$ and fixed orthonormal system and bath coordinates. Write $M_n$ for the complex system matrices, $E_{ij}=|i\rangle\langle j|$, and let $\phi_{ij}\in M_m$ be fixed bath operators with $\phi_{ji}=\phi_{ij}^{\dagger}$ and, for each $i,j$, either $\phi_{ij}=0$ or $\operatorname{Tr}\phi_{ij}=1$. Define
--   $$
--   \mathcal A_\phi(X)=\sum_{i,j}X_{ij}E_{ij}\otimes\phi_{ij},\qquad
--   \Phi_{U,\phi}(X)=\operatorname{Tr}_B\bigl[U\mathcal A_\phi(X)U^{\dagger}\bigr].
--   $$
--   Here $U$ is a joint unitary and the bath is the second tensor factor. A scalar matrix $R$ is admissible when it is Hermitian, $\sum_i R_{ii}=1$, and $\mathcal A_\phi(R)$ is a positive semidefinite trace-one matrix. Zero bath operators annihilate their corresponding matrix units on every input.
--
--    Assume that the same fixed family $\phi$ has the following property: for every joint unitary $U$, the map $\Phi_{U,\phi}$ is completely positive on all system matrices. Fix an admissible $R$; this retains the initial-state setting of the enclosing necessity proof. Complete positivity here does not require trace preservation. Let $i\sim j$ be the equivalence relation generated by the nonzero entries $\phi_{ij}\ne0$, retaining isolated indices. Write $[i]$ for the component of $i$. There is an operator $C_\alpha\in M_m$ for each component $\alpha$ such that
--   $$
--   i\not\sim j\Longrightarrow\phi_{ij}=0,\qquad
--   i\sim j\Longrightarrow\phi_{ij}\in\{0,C_{[i]}\}.
--   $$
--   Thus $[\phi_{ij}]$ is a direct sum over its connected components with one common nonzero-entry value per component. The common operator may be zero for a wholly zero singleton; it is not asserted to be a density matrix. This is the block structure needed in the necessity argument.
-- source:
--   Vanishing quantum discord is necessary and sufficient for completely positive maps, arXiv:0808.0175v2, PDF p. 3, Lemma 3

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Advance50_P40

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Advance50.P40

/-- Lemma 3, PDF pp. 3-4, under the all-unitary CP necessity hypothesis.
Components determine the direct sum; within a component every entry is zero
or one common operator. A zero singleton may have common operator zero,
and no density-matrix property is asserted for the common operators. -/
theorem lemma3_block_constant {n m : ℕ} [NeZero n] [NeZero m]
    (phi : BathFamily n m) (hphi : IsSLFamily phi)
    (R : SystemMatrix n) (hR : IsSLAdmissibleInput phi R) (hcp : AllUnitaryCP phi) :
    ∃ common : Quotient (operatorComponent phi) → SystemMatrix m,
      (∀ i j, ¬ (operatorComponent phi).r i j → phi i j = 0) ∧
      ∀ i j, (operatorComponent phi).r i j →
        phi i j = 0 ∨ phi i j = common (Quotient.mk (operatorComponent phi) i) := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Advance50.P40

end
